# Diagnostic output folder — PNG/NetCDF dumps written by probe/plot scripts.
# Excluded wholesale (incl. the former fv3_visual baselines): full-resolution
# visual-regression PNGs/NetCDFs are inspected from local working copies, NOT
# tracked. EXCEPTION (see CLAUDE.md "Validation"): the *tiny deterministic
# numeric* references under `tests/visual_baselines/` (a ~2 KB downsampled .npy +
# a JSON hash manifest) ARE tracked — they are test fixtures consumed by
# `scripts/validate/visual_regression.py --check`, not runtime artifacts.
diagnostics/
!tests/visual_baselines/

# Diagnostic plots dropped at repo root by ad-hoc scripts.
# Tracked diagnostic PNGs live under `diagnostics/` and are still
# allowed because these patterns are anchored to the repo root with `/`.
/*.png
/*.pdf
/*.svg

# Local-only research-PDF stash (papers consulted while planning).
# See CLAUDE.md "Code Hygiene Rules" — never committed.
docs/references/
# Local-only oracle source clones consulted for faithfulness audits
# (e.g. ecmwf-ifs/openifs for the Bechtold convection audit) — never committed.
ifs-source/

# Exceptions: the `.nc` files under
# `src/legoesm/atmosphere/physics/radiation/rrtmgp/optics/rrtmgp_data/`
# are package-bundled optics tables that must be tracked for RRTMGP
# radiation to work.  The `src/legoesm/ml/data/` *.py files are
# library source code that happened to match the `data/` exclude.
# Both have been tracked in history despite matching the patterns
# above; add narrow, extension-scoped negations so only the real
# package contents survive (NOT transient `.nc`, `.zarr`,
# `__pycache__/`, etc. a user might create under the directory).
!src/legoesm/atmosphere/physics/radiation/rrtmgp/optics/rrtmgp_data/*.nc
# Exception: SCM jax_scm-oracle benchmark NetCDFs (committed asset; see
# scripts/run_jax_scm_oracle.py + scripts/setup_jax_scm_oracle.sh).
!tests/validation/scm_oracle/*.nc
# Exception: the checked-in EC-site (flux-tower) validation example NetCDFs —
# a losslessly compressed model+obs asset (~34 MB) so the publication figure
# regenerates from the repo alone.  See docs/land/ec_site_evaluation_runbook.md.
!scripts/validate/ec_site_example_data/*.nc
# Exception: the trimmed EC-site DRIVER NetCDFs (analysis-window subset, model-
# consumed variables only, float64, annotated; ~30 MB) so the model itself can be
# re-run from the repo alone (runbook section B).  Built by
# scripts/data/build_ec_site_example_drivers.py.
!scripts/validate/ec_site_example_drivers/*.nc
# Exception: the vendored CLM-ML-JAX RSL psihat look-up table — committed MODEL
# DATA (~187 KB), a required input the canopy turbulence reads, not a runtime
# output.  Ships with the land package so legoESM needs no external clm-ml-jax.
!packages/land/legoesm/land/canopy/clm_ml_backend/multilayer_canopy/data/*.nc
# `!src/legoesm/ml/data/` is the minimum un-ignore needed for git to
# descend into the directory (since `data/` above ignores it).  That
# ALONE would allow arbitrary non-`.py` files in.  Re-ignore
# everything inside (including ALL nested subpaths via `**`), then
# re-allow:
#   1. All subdirectories at any depth (so git can descend to find
#      `.py` children).
#   2. All `.py` files at any depth.
# Ordering is critical — later patterns override earlier ones, so
# the `!` rules must come AFTER the re-ignore rule.
!src/legoesm/ml/data/
src/legoesm/ml/data/**
!src/legoesm/ml/data/**/
!src/legoesm/ml/data/**/*.py

